  "notes": [
    "IDs are sorted full module-created describe deltas, excluding explicitly named prerequisite nodes. Actual runtime output must match the complete owner entry, not only a common subset.",
    "Equal role keys require identical names across available owners. Additional roles preserve existing structures; null means module unavailable, never a pass for that module.",
    "Group names are verified by owner construction scans where public inspection does not expose them. TS ackDriver group is s1/ackDriver; Python and Rust have no corresponding group.",
    "Python outboundBytes is encoded bytes, unlike TS/Rust outbound envelopes. Python issues and TS/Rust errors are distinct outputs; neither is relabeled as the other."
  ],
  "boundaryError": "name must not start or end with ':'"
}
